```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Order is saved"] --> B["Load account, contact, line items, pricing, warehouse, shipping, tax, and cases"]
    B --> C{"Order activated"}
    C -->|Yes| D["Set activated stage"]
    C -->|No| E{"Rush or standard order"}
    D --> E
    E --> F["Set order type stage or continue for an unknown type"]
    F --> G{"Account tier and credit hold"}
    G --> H["Set account or credit stage where applicable"]
    H --> I{"Stock available and shipping region"}
    I --> J["Set stock or shipping stage where applicable"]
    J --> K{"Discount, tax, and open cases"}
    K --> L["Set discount, tax, or case stage where applicable"]
    L --> M{"Delivery timing, carrier, and contact email"}
    M --> N["Set final routing stage and reserve each line item"]
    N --> O["Send confirmation, post updates, schedule delivery, log fulfilment, and mark fulfilled"]
```

The flow starts after an Order is created or updated, performs a series of lookups, and then evaluates fulfilment conditions such as activation, order type, account details, stock, shipping, discounts, tax, cases, delivery, carrier, and notification eligibility. Along the way, applicable branches update `Fulfilment_Stage__c`; it then reserves stock for each line item, sends notifications, calls delivery and logging subflows, and marks the Order as `Fulfilled`.
